:"","caption":"Aspen Acres put in","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Cody Redmond","poi_id":"108053","photo_date":"2023-06-07T04:29:06.000Z","updated_at":"2023-06-07T04:29:06.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/SHToxo0rDr22T4gP2pnuH","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/SHToxo0rDr22T4gP2pnuH"}},{"id":"sdnxMLEqGuSkv6mMYJ68B","ext":"jpg","post_id":"VhCFuMf5bH6KAUbVIA7eY","description":"This is downstream side of bridge. Small Eddy on the Right (north) side for Kayaks, Rafts will have to portage. \n","caption":"Low bridge ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Cody Redmond","poi_id":"T31eSIMHxt6PaBfRateQQ","photo_date":"2023-06-07T04:29:06.000Z","updated_at":"2023-06-07T04:29:06.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/sdnxMLEqGuSkv6mMYJ68B","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/sdnxMLEqGuSkv6mMYJ68B"}}],"detail":{"id":"1882","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"None","description":"One of the more scenic rivers in northern Utah. The run rates Class II - III- with some wood avoidance and is +/- 9 miles in length.\n\nBeautiful. Ideal for inflatables and light weight kayaks. Two mandatory portages.\n\nSeveral runnable drops. Ideal level 600 cfs, runnable down to ~450 CFS and 1000+ CFS is rowdy.\n\nRiver Access is an issue.  There are threats to this river access from Private Landowners.\n\nAlthough unsigned, there is a DNR river access through the Aspen Acres (Shoshone Rd) green gate.\n\nPark in the large dirt pull out on the north side of the road and hike down to the river.\n\nThis launch is just above where Smith and Morehouse enters and increases the size of the Weber.\n\nThe New Lane Road takeout is just downstream from a dam that diverts 3/4 of the river into a canal.\n\nFlow probability forecast: [https://water.weather.gov/ahps2/probability\\_information.php?wfo=slc&gage=oawu1](https://water.weather.gov/ahps2/probability_information.php?wfo=slc&gage=oawu1)\n\nIN 2017 USAC won a supreme court case on this section of river (Holiday Park to Echo Resevoir) The court ruling is here:  [https://wildlife.utah.gov/special-weber-river-rules.html](https://wildlife.utah.gov/special-weber-river-rules.html)\n\nIn basic terms we have a right to the water way and the ground on which it flows, up to the high water mark. Access to the river must be through public access points or private with permission from the land owner.  Please obey trespassing signage.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"10.8","correlations":[{"reachID":"1882","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"400","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"1200"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"WEBER RIVER NEAR OAKLEY, UT","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"10128500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"369","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"6.46","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"40.7371721","longitude":"-111.2479652"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/10128500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/10128500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 400 - 1200 cfs  Comment: Ideal flow is ~600\n\nMigration Errors: \nSingle range is valid but doesn't provide low/medium/high runnable\nThere is one comment for all of low/medium/high runnable.","comment":"Gauge (162 sq.mi. drainage) is just above the put-in for this reach, thus